{"subject": "maths", "level": "ibdp", "topic_display": "Vectors (HL)", "topic_slug": "vectors-hl", "theme": "maths-grid", "adventure_n": 1, "title": "Dot Product and Angles", "emoji": "➡️", "welcome_lead": "Probe directions: master the dot product and the angle it reveals.", "meta_desc": "HL Maths adventure on vector dot product, magnitudes and angle calculations.", "final_note": "Zero dot product means perpendicular vectors!", "concepts": [{"term": "Vector", "def": "Quantity with magnitude and direction."}, {"term": "Magnitude", "def": "|a| = √(a1^2 + a2^2 + a3^2)."}, {"term": "Dot product", "def": "a·b = a1b1 + a2b2 + a3b3."}, {"term": "Angle formula", "def": "a·b = |a||b| cos θ."}, {"term": "Perpendicular", "def": "a·b = 0 when a ⟂ b."}, {"term": "Unit vector", "def": "â = a / |a|, length 1."}], "walkthroughs": [{"tag": "dot", "h2": "Compute Dot Product", "body_html": "<p>a = (2, 3, 1), b = (1, -1, 4). Find a·b.</p><p>= 2(1) + 3(-1) + 1(4) = 2 - 3 + 4 = 3.</p>"}, {"tag": "angle", "h2": "Angle Between Vectors", "body_html": "<p>Above, |a| = √14, |b| = √18. cos θ = 3/√(14×18) ≈ 0.189.</p><p>θ ≈ 79.1°.</p>"}, {"tag": "perp", "h2": "Test Perpendicularity", "body_html": "<p>Are (1, 2, 3) and (2, -1, 0) perpendicular?</p><p>Dot = 2 - 2 + 0 = 0, so yes.</p>"}], "mcqs": [{"q": "If a·b = 0, then:", "options": [["a is perpendicular to b", 1], ["a is parallel to b", 0], ["a = -b", 0], ["a = 0", 0]]}, {"q": "|a| for a = (3, 4, 0)?", "options": [["5", 1], ["7", 0], ["12", 0], ["25", 0]]}], "numericals": [{"q": "Dot product of (1,2,3) and (4,5,6)?", "options": [32, 28, 26, 20], "answer": 32}], "free_texts": [{"q": "Name for a vector of length 1?", "answer": "unit vector"}]}